# Kafka Resilience — Manual Test Scenarios

This section documents the manual scenarios used to validate the reliability mechanisms implemented around Kafka, the Transactional Outbox Pattern and the idempotent consumer.

The goal of these tests is to verify the behavior of the system under real failure conditions rather than only validating the happy path.

---

## Test Overview

| Test    | Scenario                                  | Validates                                 | Status |
| ------- | ----------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | ------ |
| TEST-01 | Consumer failure → retries → DLT          | Retry policy and Dead Letter Topic        | ✅      |
| TEST-02 | Missing `eventId`                         | Non-retryable errors → immediate DLT      | ✅      |
| TEST-03 | Same `eventId` received twice             | Idempotent Consumer                       | ✅      |
| TEST-04 | Business failure after idempotency insert | Transaction rollback                      | ✅      |
| TEST-05 | Kafka unavailable during publication      | Transactional Outbox                      | ✅      |
| TEST-06 | One Kafka broker unavailable              | Replication / availability with 2 ISR     | ✅      |
| TEST-07 | Insufficient ISR                          | `acks=all` + `min.insync.replicas=2`      | ✅      |
| TEST-08 | Broker restart                            | Replica catch-up and ISR recovery         | ✅      |
| TEST-09 | Locate record / partition / replica       | Kafka storage and replication diagnostics | ✅ / 🔎 |
| TEST-10 | Kafka ACK then application crash          | Outbox at-least-once redelivery           | ⏳      |

