# TEST-01 — Consumer Failure → Retry → DLT

## Objective

Verify that a retryable consumer failure results in:

```text
initial attempt
→ retry 1
→ retry 2
→ retry 3
→ Dead Letter Topic
```

The configured backoff is:

```java
FixedBackOff backOff = new FixedBackOff(1000L, 3);
```

This means:

```text
1 initial attempt
+ 3 retries
= 4 total attempts
```

---

## Temporary Test Preparation

Temporarily add the following block inside:

```text
OrderEventConsumer.consume()
```

before the idempotent processor:

```java
if (record.value().contains(
        "99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999"
)) {
    throw new RuntimeException(
            "Intentional Retry + DLT test failure"
    );
}
```

The UUID is reserved only for this manual failure-injection test.

---

## Action

Create an order using the reserved UUID:

```bash
curl -X POST \
  http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999
```

---

## Expected Result

The consumer must fail four times:

```text
Attempt 1
↓
Retry 1
↓
Retry 2
↓
Retry 3
↓
Retries exhausted
↓
order-events-secure.DLT
```

---

## Verify the DLT

```bash
docker exec kafka-1 /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh \
  --bootstrap-server kafka-1:29092 \
  --topic order-events-secure.DLT \
  --from-beginning
```

The payload containing:

```text
99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999
```

must be present.

---

## What This Proves

A retryable consumer failure does not silently lose the event.

```text
processing failure
→ retries
→ retries exhausted
→ record quarantined in DLT
```

---

## Cleanup

Remove the temporary failure block after the test.

It must not remain in production code.

