# TEST-02 — Missing `eventId` → Immediate DLT

## Objective

Verify that a structurally invalid Kafka record is **not retried unnecessarily**.

A missing `eventId` cannot be repaired by retrying the exact same record.

---

## Consumer Protection

The consumer checks the required Kafka header:

```java
Header eventIdHeader =
        record.headers().lastHeader("eventId");

if (eventIdHeader == null) {
    throw new MissingEventIdException(
            "Missing required Kafka header: eventId"
    );
}
```

The error handler declares this exception as non-retryable:

```java
errorHandler.addNotRetryableExceptions(
        MissingEventIdException.class
);
```

---

## Action

Produce a message manually without the required header:

```bash
echo '{"test":"missing-event-id"}' | docker exec -i kafka-1 \
  /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-producer.sh \
  --bootstrap-server kafka-1:29092 \
  --topic order-events-secure
```

---

## Expected Result

```text
record received
↓
eventId header missing
↓
MissingEventIdException
↓
NO retry
↓
DLT immediately
```

There must not be three:

```text
Record in retry and not yet recovered
```

messages.

---

## Verify the DLT

```bash
docker exec kafka-1 /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh \
  --bootstrap-server kafka-1:29092 \
  --topic order-events-secure.DLT \
  --from-beginning \
  --timeout-ms 5000 | grep 'missing-event-id'
```

Expected:

```text
{"test":"missing-event-id"}
```

---

## What This Proves

The application distinguishes between recoverable and non-recoverable errors.

```text
temporary failure
→ retry

structural invalid message
→ DLT directly
```

This prevents useless retries for records that can never become valid.

