# TEST-09 — Locate Record, Partition, Offset and Local Replica

## Objective

Inspect where a specific Kafka record is stored.

This is mainly a diagnostic / educational scenario.

---

## Step 1 — Find Partition and Offset

For:

```text
66666666-6666-6666-6666-666666666669
```

run:

```bash
docker exec kafka-1 /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh \
  --bootstrap-server kafka-1:29092 \
  --topic order-events-secure \
  --from-beginning \
  --timeout-ms 5000 \
  --property print.partition=true \
  --property print.offset=true | \
  grep '66666666-6666-6666-6666-666666666669'
```

Observed:

```text
Partition:1
Offset:25
```

Therefore:

```text
Topic     = order-events-secure
Partition = 1
Offset    = 25
```

---

## Step 2 — Verify Partition Replicas

```bash
docker exec kafka-1 /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-topics.sh \
  --bootstrap-server kafka-1:29092 \
  --describe \
  --topic order-events-secure
```

Example:

```text
Partition: 1
Leader:    3
Replicas:  3,1,2
Isr:       1,2,3
```

This means Partition 1 exists on:

```text
broker 1
broker 2
broker 3
```

---

## Step 3 — Locate Partition Storage on Broker 3

```bash
docker exec kafka-3 sh -lc \
'find /tmp /var /opt -type d -name "order-events-secure-1" 2>/dev/null'
```

Observed:

```text
/tmp/kafka-logs/order-events-secure-1
```

Kafka therefore stores the local Partition 1 replica in this directory.

---

## Optional — Inspect the Local Kafka Log

```bash
docker exec kafka-3 sh -lc \
'/opt/kafka/bin/kafka-dump-log.sh \
 --files /tmp/kafka-logs/order-events-secure-1/*.log \
 --print-data-log 2>/dev/null | \
 grep "66666666-6666-6666-6666-666666666669"'
```

This can be used to inspect whether the exact record exists inside the broker's local partition log.

---

## What This Proves

A Kafka record belongs to:

```text
one topic
one partition
one offset inside that partition
```

It does **not** exist in all three partitions.

Instead:

```text
record
↓
Partition 1
↓
Partition 1 replicated across brokers
```

With replication factor 3:

```text
Broker 1 → Partition 1 replica
Broker 2 → Partition 1 replica
Broker 3 → Partition 1 replica
```

