# TEST-10 — Kafka ACK Then Crash Before `processed=true`

## Status

```text
NOT EXECUTED YET
```

## Objective

Validate the classic at-least-once delivery window of the Transactional Outbox.

---

## Failure Window

The Relay currently performs:

```java
kafkaTemplate.send(record).get();

entity.setProcessed(true);

outboxRepository.save(entity);
```

There is a small failure window between:

```text
Kafka ACK
```

and:

```text
processed=true committed in database
```

---

## Scenario to Test

```text
Outbox processed=false
↓
Relay sends event
↓
Kafka accepts event
↓
Kafka ACK
↓
APPLICATION CRASH
↓
processed=true never committed
```

After restart:

```text
Outbox still says processed=false
↓
Relay publishes same event again
↓
same eventId
↓
consumer receives duplicate
↓
processed_messages detects duplicate
↓
business logic not executed again
```

---

## Why This Test Matters

This demonstrates why the architecture is described as:

```text
Transactional Outbox
+
At-Least-Once Delivery
+
Idempotent Consumer
```

and not as guaranteed end-to-end exactly-once delivery.

